# Mobile Responsiveness Implementation Plan

The goal is to make the entire SkillArena gamified learning platform fully responsive on mobile devices and tablets. Currently, the app has basic styles, but it lacks cohesive mobile behaviors (like responsive sidebars, grid collapses, font sizing, and optimized spacing).

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> Please review how the Sidebar and Navbar will behave on mobile. Since this is a dashboard application, I propose changing the Sidebar into a **Bottom Tab Navigation** (or a collapsible hamburger menu) for mobile devices. Let me know which you prefer! (I will proceed with a Bottom Tab Navigation for a "mobile app" feel unless you specify otherwise).

## Proposed Changes

We will systematically update the CSS files to add `@media (max-width: 768px)` blocks to ensure grid layouts gracefully collapse, paddings adjust, and navigation becomes mobile-friendly.

### 1. Global & Layout Components
#### [MODIFY] `src/app/globals.css`
- Reduce root font-sizes slightly for smaller viewports to prevent text overflow.
- Adjust global `--space-*` variables dynamically if needed.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/Landing.css`
- Ensure the hero section title scales down properly.
- Stack the features grid to a single column on mobile.
- Adjust footer link columns.

#### [MODIFY] `src/components/layout/Sidebar.css`
- Transform the fixed sidebar into a fixed **bottom navigation bar** for screens `< 768px`.
- Hide user profile details (avatar, name) in the bottom bar, showing only icons for navigation to save space.

#### [MODIFY] `src/components/layout/Navbar.css`
- Adjust the top navbar to handle logo and profile/actions without overflowing.
- Add a hamburger menu if necessary, or let the bottom bar handle main navigation.

### 2. Feature & Page Components
#### [MODIFY] `src/features/courses/components/CourseCatalog.css`
- Change `.catalog-grid` from multi-column grid to a single column on mobile.
- Make the search and filter header stack vertically.

#### [MODIFY] `src/features/courses/components/LessonView.css`
- Ensure the video player and sidebar content stack vertically instead of side-by-side.

#### [MODIFY] `src/features/auth/components/AuthForms.css`
- Reduce form paddings and ensure inputs span full width without horizontal scrolling.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(dashboard)/profile/Profile.css`
- Change profile grid (stats vs details) to a single column.
- Center align avatar and user details.

#### [MODIFY] `src/app/(dashboard)/DashboardLayout.css`
- Adjust padding for `.dashboard-content` to `var(--space-md)` or smaller.
- Remove `margin-left: var(--sidebar-width)` on mobile, adding `padding-bottom` to account for the bottom navigation bar.

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run `npm run build` to ensure no CSS syntax errors are introduced.

### Manual Verification
- Start the app with `npm run dev` and test the following pages using Chrome DevTools Device Mode (iPhone 12 Pro dimensions):
  - Landing Page
  - Login/Signup
  - Course Catalog
  - Course Player
  - Profile & Dashboard
- Verify that horizontal scrolling is eliminated.
- Verify that the bottom navigation bar behaves correctly on mobile.
